The overall message of the two meetings

The first file teaches “how Dynatrace monitoring is configured” — synthetic monitors, dashboard tags, RUM, application detection, and monitoring modes.

The second file turns that into “how we operate Dynatrace” — onboarding servers, firewall/OneAgent installation, production approvals, enabling/disabling monitoring, troubleshooting, and deciding when a Dynatrace problem actually needs escalation.

So if you're using these meetings to learn your responsibilities, I'd think of the workflow as:

Server/application change → approval → firewall → OneAgent → Dynatrace configuration → enable monitoring → validate → tracker → ongoing dashboard/problem monitoring → troubleshoot/escalate when needed.
